# Evidence content must never enter an image any more than it enters git.
_evidence_root/
**/_evidence_root/

.git/
.github/
# **/ prefix is load-bearing: unlike .gitignore, Docker's ignore matcher does
# NOT treat a bare pattern as implicitly recursive, and the only COPY in the
# Dockerfile ships tools/ wholesale -- a bare `__pycache__/` here misses every
# tools/**/__pycache__ that `make test`/`make coverage` actually write,
# baking stale .pyc files into the image the Dockerfile's own header comment
# calls "reproducible". Confirmed by building the image from a tree with real
# cache artifacts under tools/ and finding them inside the exported image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
build/
dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
docs/patches/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
